sequenceDiagram
    participant UART as GPS UART
    participant GT as gpsTask
    participant TG as TinyGPSPlus
    participant NP as nmea_parser
    participant MTX as stateMutex
    participant SNK as SD / TCP sinks

    Note over GT: line assembly needs no lock<br/>the UART and line buffer<br/>belong only to this task
    UART->>GT: bytes, until '\n'
    GT->>SNK: logSentence(line)
    Note over GT,SNK: outside the lock -- SD write is<br/>the slowest step in the path

    GT->>MTX: take (per sentence)
    activate MTX
    GT->>TG: encode(line)
    GT->>NP: handleRawSentence(line)
    NP->>NP: parse GSV / GSA<br/>update satellite table, fix mode
    GT->>MTX: give
    deactivate MTX
    Note over GT,MTX: ~50 sentences/sec, each its own<br/>lock/unlock -- not one lock<br/>around the whole UART drain

    loop every completed fix epoch
        Note over GT: epoch key = receiver's own UTC stamp,<br/>not TinyGPSPlus isUpdated()<br/>(reading a value clears its flag)
        GT->>MTX: take
        GT->>GT: accumulate trip stats,<br/>HDOP/speed history, fixSecs[]
        GT->>MTX: give
        GT->>SNK: write track CSV row (unlocked)
    end
